const tests = done('tests:' + K) || await agent(RULES + '\nRole: test writer (Engineer), rules.md section (d), for ' + ROW + ': ' + SPEC + '. Branch ' + TB + ', ' + WTNEW('harness-' + K + '-tests', 'tests-' + K, 'origin/main') + '. You create ' + NEWTEST + ' (new) and edit ONLY the three retired literals and the one docstring (:45) of INTERFACE 6 in ' + SEEDTEST + '. Tests are the spec: write the cases (a) to (k) of INTERFACE 5, one pytest function each, fixtures in tmp_path, no network. You are NOT the builder. The file header quotes the three spec paragraphs above word for word and the picked details D1 to D5 and the four rulings of the amendment (D2, D3, D5). TRAP: scripts/specfactory/rule_pins_tests.py treats a test file as pinned if it contains ANY token of the form R-###-## (R, hyphen, three digits, hyphen, two digits) and then rejects "Rule pins: none"; the file must contain NO such token anywhere.\n' + IFACE + '\n' + BASE_NOTE + '\nRED/GREEN EXPECTATION on the base tree: (a) undertest half, (b), (d), (e), (f), (g), (h), (j), (k) and the --gated half of (i) must be RED for the stated reason (the comma id is unsplit by undertest_warn and the acceptance-verdict handler; the shell reject detail is the bare log tail; argparse rejects --gated, so there is no seeded line and no baseline_cache/<HEAD>.json): paste the failing assertion line of each verbatim (file:line and message) and say, for each, that the reason is the stated one and not a fixture defect; (a) acceptance-ids half, (c), the single-increment control of (k) and (i) non-merge half must be GREEN on the base (positive controls; paste the recorded current bytes of (c) and the pytest summary line). The three retired literals (the docstring edit cannot be red) in test_gate_cache_seed.py are RED on base after your edit (the old line lacks "suites from"); state that, paste their failing lines, and the builder turns them green; report the TD text of INTERFACE 6 (positive control: the three tests pass against the new line and fail against the old: run them both ways). A control that is red on the base is a defect of your test: fix it before you push. Thresholds: none invented. Pre-gate: ' + PREGATE('<worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + '; red tests make the test step REJECT by design: quote that line and say the other steps are OK. Push the tests branch, then wt.py done. Report ok, branch, sha, summary (the failing assertion line per red test, the control lines, the summary line, the TD row text for the retired literals), red_ids.', { label: 'tests:' + K, phase: 'Tests', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, tests }
if (!(tests && tests.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'tests:' + K }

phase('Build')
const mkBuild = (extra, retry) => done('build:' + K) || agent(RULES + '\nRole: Doer (rules.md section (a)) for ' + ROW + ': ' + SPEC + '. Branch ' + (retry ? BB2 : BB) + ', ' + WTNEW(retry ? 'harness-' + K + '-b2' : 'harness-' + K, 'build-' + K, 'origin/main') + (retry ? ' (RETRY after a ruling: the first attempt\'s worktree harness-' + K + ' and branch ' + BB + ' exist and are NOT reused; this is a fresh tree and branch, and your report\'s branch field is ' + BB2 + ')' : '') + '; merge origin/' + tests.branch + rulingMerge() + extra + '.\nEdit ONLY ' + PRODUCT + ', ' + SHELL + ' (one line in each of the two reject branches, INTERFACE 1; change nothing else in the shell) and ' + RULESMD + ' (one sentence APPENDED to the Push bullet; keep intact the substring pinned by test_P_rules_md_push_bullet_names_the_seed_cache_line, test_gate_cache_seed.py:430, and run that test; INTERFACE 1). Use the shell form of INTERFACE 1 exactly (`D="${VERDICT#REJECT}"; D="${D# }"` then `${D:+$D }` before the log tail; a single-id bare REJECT yields today\'s detail unchanged). The test files are the test writer\'s, you never edit them. Implement INTERFACE 2 and 3 exactly: split on commas as footprint_check does (reuse the same expression, not a new helper unless the three call sites need one), resolve increments per id as today, leave acceptance_ids as it is (header V2), print the one-line verdict `' + LINE_REJ + '` (or `' + LINE_REJ0 + '` when no failing id maps to a named piece; several increments give one WARN line, details joined by `; `) and the `undertest <id>: ...` lines exactly as D2 fixes them (the sub-command\'s stdout stays ONE line), make seed_cache take the gated sha with the defaults and the ancestor rule of D3 and print `' + LINE_SEED + '`; the baseline lookup stays _find_cached_by_inputs. About 40 lines; no new config, flag or layer other than `--gated`. A rule neither the spec text nor the interface gives stops you with stop_reason "spec-gap: <what>" (and, quoting the line, if a ruling contradicts something in merge_gate.sh).\n' + IFACE + '\n' + BASE_NOTE + '\nDone when: ' + NEWTEST + ' is green with its controls and ' + NEIGHBOURS.join(', ') + ' are green (paste the summary lines of each; a failure present on origin/main too is reported, not blamed); git diff against origin/main shows only ' + PRODUCT + ', ' + SHELL + ' (two lines) and ' + RULESMD + ' changed besides the merged tests (paste git diff --stat); python3 -m py_compile ' + PRODUCT + ' passes. Pre-gate: ' + PREGATE('<worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + ' must end PRE_GATE verdict OK; quote the verdict. Push the branch (it is NOT merged to main by you), then wt.py done. Report ok, branch, sha, summary (all of the pasted items above), red_ids, parked.', { label: 'build:' + K, phase: 'Build', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'doer', model: 'sonnet' })
const build = await withRuling(mkBuild)
out = { ...out, build }
if (!(build && build.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'build:' + K }

phase('Check')
const check = SKIP['check:' + K] ? { pass: true, evidence: 'skipped: check ok' } : await agent(RULES + '\nRole: gate agent (Engineer), rules.md section (c), read-only, ' + WTNEW('chk-harness-' + K, 'chk-' + K, 'origin/' + build.branch) + ' (push nothing; you close the tree yourself as your last step). Spec: ' + SPEC + '.\n' + IFACE + '\n' + BASE_NOTE + '\n(1) The diff of origin/' + build.branch + ' against its merge base touches only ' + PRODUCT + ', ' + SHELL + ' (exactly two changed lines, paste the diff) and ' + RULESMD + ' plus, from the merged test branch, ' + NEWTEST + ' and ' + SEEDTEST + '; list every other file (blocking). py_compile of ' + PRODUCT + ' passes. The rules.md diff is ONE added sentence in the Push bullet naming `seed-cache` and `--gated` (paste the diff). (2) Run ' + NEWTEST + ' and ' + NEIGHBOURS.join(', ') + ': PASS/FAIL per file with counts, all green. (3) POSITIVE CONTROL: run ' + NEWTEST + ' against the base product (swap git show origin/main:' + PRODUCT + ' into your tree, run, swap back; never commit): the cases (a) undertest half, (b), (d), (e), (f), (g), (h), (j), (k) and the --gated half of (i) go red again; (c), the acceptance-ids half of (a) and the non-merge half of (i) stay green; list them. (4) BYTE-IDENTICAL SINGLE ID (and one line of verdict for a combined id: the stdout of acceptance-verdict for `A,B` with a failing test of B is exactly one line, `REJECT B: ...`, paste it with `wc -l`): with the new product run `python3 ' + PRODUCT + ' acceptance-verdict B --pieces <fixture toml> --ids-file <f> --pytest-log <failing log>` and the same with the base product: the two stdouts are identical (paste both with `cmp`), and the same for the increment id. (5) A COMBINED GATE RUN: run the real merge_gate.sh on a fixture repo as ' + A94 + ' _gate does with the piece list "A,B" (two fixture pieces with passing acceptance): paste the one `GATE acceptance` line it prints (OK output byte-identical to the single-id line) and the `undertest` lines, and say whether the old `no pytest-collectible acceptance ids for piece A,B` line is gone; then with a failing test in B paste the reject line (its detail begins with `B: `) (informational numbers; ' + FIXTURE_GATE_S + ' s per fixture gate). (6) SEED: in a scratch merge root run `seed-cache --gated` on a --no-ff fixture merge and paste the line (`seeded <n> suites from <gated> for <HEAD>`); then without --gated; then with a side-branch sha (paste the skip line). (7) PRE-GATE: run ' + PREGATE('<this worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + ' and paste EVERY line; it must end PRE_GATE verdict OK; list each WARN. LAST STEP: close your tree with python3 ~/Projects/ouroboros-manifold/scripts/specfactory/wt.py done <this worktree path> <sha>, where <sha> is `git rev-parse origin/main` run in that tree; paste the wt.py line. Report pass, blocking, evidence (every PASS/FAIL line) and decisive_line (the one line that decides pass or fail).', { label: 'check:' + K, phase: 'Check', schema: VERDICT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, check }
if (!(check && check.pass)) return { ...out, stopped: 'check:' + K }
return { ...out, next: 'a landing clerk lands ' + build.branch + ' (merge origin/' + tests.branch + ' and origin/' + build.branch + ', pre-gate, merge gate, records commit with the TD row texts of the writer and the ruler); no landing was done by this script' }
